 "$schema": "com.minomobi.cad.assembly#v1",
 "name": "gripper-stroke",
 "_": "Parallel-jaw robot gripper, v5, coaxial: ISO 9409-1-50-4-M6 flange → NEMA 17 pancake stepper with an integrated Tr8×2 screw → flange nut in a carriage that the housing aligns (skid on the bed, arm tips at the walls) → two pivot arms keyed into the carriage → four 27 mm links on bronze bushings, one above and one below the mid-plane → two one-piece finger slides in the mid-plane, each on an MGN9 block on one rail lying on the bed beyond the front wall, each ending in a 16 × 12 tenon for the customer’s finger. The screw axis, the flange centre, the rail, the links’ plane of symmetry and the tenons share the line x = 0, z = 0. 96 × 54 × 104 mm case, tenons to y = 143. The physical stroke: the screw is driven at 5 rpm, a screw mate moves the carriage 2 mm per turn (y = 61.68 open → 75.63 closed in 6.978 turns, 83.7 s), fixed mates carry the nut and the arms, and the links swing the slides in: the example jaws from 36 mm apart to touching. Sweep with period 83.7 s; beyond it the nut runs on, as it would.",
